    "approach": "The problem does not require any input. We simply compute the four required results using the fixed numbers 888 and 444. For each test case (if a test count is supplied) we output: 888+444, 888-444, 888/444 formatted to two decimal places, and 888*444, each on its own line. The computation is O(1) per test case.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(T) where T is the number of test cases (default 1).",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1) additional space.",
    "code": {
      "C": "",
      "C++": "",
      "Java": "import java.io.*;\npublic class Main{\n    public static void main(String[] args){\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        sb.append(888+444).append('\\n');\n        sb.append(888-444).append('\\n');\n        sb.append(String.format(\"%.2f\", 888.0/444)).append('\\n');\n        sb.append(888*444).append('\\n');\n        System.out.print(sb.toString());\n    }\n}",
